.\" -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
.\" klamav-py-gui(1) — English page
.\"
.\" Maintenance conventions: same as klamav-py(1).
.\" Consistency with the parser in klamav_py/gui/app.py and with the
.\" Italian page is checked by tests/test_manpage.py.
.\"
.TH KLAMAV-PY-GUI 1 "2026-11-10" "KlamAV-Py 0.1.21" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
klamav-py-gui \- KlamAV-Py graphical interface for the ClamAV daemon
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B klamav-py-gui
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-tcp
.IR host [: port ]]
.RB [ \-\-quarantine\-dir
.IR directory ]
.RB [ \-\-scan\-target
.IR path ...]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B klamav-py-gui
is the KlamAV-Py graphical interface: manual and scheduled scans,
quarantine management, signature updates, and integration with the
Dolphin context menu.
Like
.BR klamav-py (1),
it talks to
.BR clamd (8)
through its native protocol.
.PP
The application keeps running in the system tray when the window is
closed.
With the start-in-tray setting, it starts without showing the window,
unless it receives paths to scan.
.PP
Only one instance per user is allowed: a second launch forwards the
.B \-\-scan\-target
paths to the running instance and exits immediately.
.PP
Detections that are reported but not moved (heuristic signatures and
mail archives, see
.BR klamav-py (1))
are listed in the Heuristic findings page
.RI ( Segnalazioni Euristiche ),
whichever scan found them: the scans of the window (manual, scheduled,
Real-Time) and the
.BR klamav-py (1)
command line.
Each scan records them as soon as it finds them, so they survive a scan
that is interrupted later, and the page reads them at startup, every time
it is opened and with \(lqAggiorna\(rq (refresh).
A detection leaves the list when it is deleted or acknowledged (also with
.BR "klamav\-py \-\-acknowledge" ),
or when its file is no longer there.
After checking one, it can be deleted, only if the path is still the same
regular file that was detected, or acknowledged: later scans no longer
count its content as infected.
The acknowledgement applies to the content and the signature, in any
path: an identical copy elsewhere, with the same signature, is already
acknowledged.
The same page lists the acknowledgements and revokes them.
If the register turns out to be invalid when recording, revoking or
reloading, the page says so and names the
.I acknowledged.json.corrupt-*
file where the previous acknowledgements remain, not deleted.
After deleting a message from a mail archive managed by Akonadi (KMail),
.B akonadictl fsck
may be needed.
.PP
The Scheduling page
.RI ( Pianificazione )
turns on and configures the automatic scans (interval in hours or days,
folder, excluded folders), which run while the application is open, even
only in the system tray.
Up to version 0.1.21 the packages also installed a scheduled system scan
.RB ( klamav\-scan.timer ),
now removed.
At startup the application removes its leftovers in the home, if the
unit is no longer installed: it stops the timer still loaded in the
session, removes the enablement made with
.BR "systemctl \-\-user enable" ,
its own drop-ins in
.I \%~/.config/systemd/user/klamav\-scan.service.d/
and
.I \%~/.config/systemd/user/klamav\-scan.timer.d/
(only the files with the header
.RI \(lq "Generato da KlamAV-Py" \(rq)
and the interrupted-scan state
.RI ( \%~/.local/share/klamav\-py/timer\-scan.json ),
then runs
.BR "systemctl \-\-user daemon\-reload" .
It says so once with a notification, and in the Scheduling page and on
stderr at every startup where it finds something; files written by others
in those folders stay where they are and are listed.
Folders whose permissions deny access during a scan are listed and
counted separately from errors; any other error on a folder (an I/O error,
an NFS mount that stopped responding) is listed and counted among the
errors.
These errors, and read errors on a file that are neither denied
permissions nor vanished files, are I/O faults: part of the tree was not
checked.
The outcome stays \(lqCompletata con errori\(rq (completed with errors),
but the status and the
report of the manual scan and the notification of the internal scheduled
scan say so with the same sentence as the last line of the
.BR klamav-py (1)
summary, and History counts them in a separate column.
The notifications of the manual and of the internal scheduled scan, and
the manual scan report, show a warning icon for every outcome other than
a clean scan: errors, I/O faults or a scan not completed (infections keep
their own icon).
Problems reported during a scan without a file error (for example an
invalid register of acknowledged detections) count as errors for the
outcome of both: \(lqCompletata con errori\(rq, with the number of
problems in the manual scan report.
A path to scan that does not exist, is a broken symbolic link, is neither
a folder nor a regular file, or cannot be read stops the scan.
So does a quarantine directory that cannot be used, or a clamd client
that cannot be prepared: the scan is reported as not completed, with the
reason.
The History entry of a scan that was not completed or was postponed keeps
its reason, also after the application is closed.
.PP
The quarantine directory is prepared in the background, together with the
recovery of interrupted operations: until then the Quarantine page shows
that it is loading, and an error preparing it is shown there.
The restore and delete buttons are available only once the quarantine is
loaded.
Restoring, deleting and quarantining the selected files from the Scan
page run in the background, one at a time: while one is in progress the
restore and delete buttons are disabled, and quarantining from the Scan
page asks to wait.
After an error, loading does not restart by itself: fix the directory in
Settings if needed, then press \(lqAggiorna\(rq (refresh) in the Quarantine
page; until then quarantining the selected files from the Scan page shows
the reason.
\(lqAggiorna\(rq also repeats the recovery, so an operation left half done
during the session (for example a file moved into quarantine whose index
entry could not be written) is completed without restarting.
The operations completed or rolled back by a load are listed in the
Quarantine page, with the original path and the outcome, and announced
by a tray notification if the page is not visible.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.BR \-\-socket ,
.B \-\-tcp
and
.B \-\-quarantine\-dir
only apply while Settings has no saved value: once Settings has been
saved, its value takes precedence.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Path to the clamd Unix socket.
Default:
.IR /run/clamav/clamd.ctl .
.TP
.BI \-\-tcp " host\fR[\fP:port\fR]\fP"
Connect to clamd via TCP instead of a Unix socket
(default port 3310).
Incompatible with
.BR \-\-socket .
See
.B SECURITY
in
.BR klamav-py (1)
before using it.
.TP
.BI \-\-quarantine\-dir " directory"
Quarantine directory.
Default:
.IR \%~/.local/share/klamav-py/quarantine .
.TP
.BI \-\-scan\-target " path\fR...\fP"
Scan one or more files or directories at startup or, if the application
is already running, forward them to the running instance.
The Dolphin context menu uses it to pass the whole selection in a single
invocation.
If the selection is too large to forward, the excess items are not sent
and a warning on standard error reports how many: in that case, scan the
folder that contains them instead.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory of the single-instance socket.
If it is missing or invalid, the application still starts, but without
the single-instance check, and says so.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory of the configuration file (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \%~/.config/KlamAV-Py/KlamAV-Py.conf
Settings.
Settings from the previous version, saved under the name KlamAV, are
migrated automatically on first start.
.TP
.I \%~/.local/share/klamav-py/acknowledged.json
Register of acknowledged detections, shared with
.BR klamav-py (1).
.TP
.I \%~/.local/share/klamav-py/pending-reports.json
Detections still to be evaluated, written by every scan and read by the
Findings page; see
.BR klamav-py (1).
.TP
.I \%/usr/share/applications/klamav-py.desktop
Menu entry; its name is also the application ID that Wayland and KDE use
to match the window with its icon.
.
.SH SECURITY
.SS Single instance
The single-instance socket lives in the user's runtime directory, never
in
.IR /tmp ,
and only its owner can access it; the identity of the listening process
is verified before any data is sent to it.
If the socket cannot be created, the application still starts, with a
warning: refusing to start would let whoever causes the problem block the
antivirus.
.
.SS Quarantine directory
The rules described in
.BR klamav-py (1)
apply: volatile directories are rejected, and
.BR tmpfs " and " ramfs
file systems are accepted with a warning.
.
.SS Signature updates
Updating does not run
.BR freshclam (1)
as root: it restarts the system unit through
.BR pkexec (1)
and
.BR systemctl (1)
with fixed arguments and a closed list of permitted units.
The binaries involved must be owned by root and not writable by group or
others; otherwise the operation is refused.
The outcome is verified by reading the database version back from clamd.
.PP
With clamd reached over TCP, restarting the local freshclam does not
always update the database clamd uses, and updating is disabled with an
explanation: always for a remote host (the database is updated where
clamd runs); for a loopback address, when the database version reported
by clamd differs from the one in the directory set by
.B DatabaseDirectory
in the local
.BR freshclam.conf (5),
or
.I /var/lib/clamav
if it is not set (for example clamd in a container).
Host names other than
.I localhost
are not resolved and count as remote.
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR klamav-py (1),
.BR clamd (8),
.BR freshclam (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
